    <section id="mistakes">
      <h2>Mistakes that cause rejected Zoho e-invoices</h2>
      <ul class="know">
        <li><b>Missing customer TRNs.</b> This is the most common problem. Run a report of business customers with no TRN. Fix those first.</li>
        <li><b>Names that do not match.</b> Your customer's legal name must match its registration. A trading name will not do. Check yours too.</li>
        <li><b>Free-text units.</b> Words like "pcs" or "boxes" may fail. Use the standard unit list your ASP accepts.</li>
        <li><b>Items with no VAT treatment.</b> Every item needs the right treatment: standard-rated, zero-rated, exempt or out of scope. Do not rely on a default.</li>
        <li><b>Editing after sending.</b> You cannot. Credit notes fix mistakes, and each one uses a transaction. Check every invoice before you send it.</li>
        <li><b>Mixing B2B and B2C.</b> Do not send consumer receipts through Peppol, and do not skip a business customer. Mark customer types clearly.</li>
        <li><b>Ignoring supplier invoices.</b> E-invoicing runs both ways. Supplier e-invoices and vendor credits arrive in Zoho Books as drafts. Someone must review them. Ask your suppliers for their Peppol IDs early.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section id="help">
      <h2>Set it up yourself, or get help?</h2>
      <p>You can do the setup yourself for free. The five steps above are enough for many businesses. If your customer and item data are clean, you may finish in an afternoon.</p>
      <p>Get help if your data is messy, if you have many customers or if you have no time to test. Our setup service costs {aed(P.help)}, one time. We check your plan so you do not pay for more than you need. We check and fix your customer TRNs, VAT codes and items. We handle the EmaraTax appointment. We send a test invoice and credit note, and we fix rejected invoices. We also show your staff how it works.</p>
      <p>Not on Zoho? Other software has its own path. TallyPrime and Wafeq have e-invoicing built in, like Zoho. QuickBooks and Excel need an outside ASP. See <a href="/tally">Tally</a>, <a href="/wafeq">Wafeq</a>, <a href="/quickbooks-online">QuickBooks Online</a> or <a href="/other-software">other software</a>.</p>
